# Build & Test Rules

## After Every Code Change
Run this build check before saying you're done:
```bash
PROJ=/Users/brianbean/Desktop/huehome-pro-v0.3.0
xcodebuild -project "$PROJ/HueHome.xcodeproj" -scheme "HueHome 1" -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' build 2>&1 | grep -E 'error:|BUILD SUCCEEDED|BUILD FAILED'
```
The scheme is `HueHome 1`, not `HueHome`. To build or test against a simulator,
prefer `./run_tests.sh` (it picks a deterministic simulator) or pass an exact
`-destination 'id=<UDID>'` — several installed simulators share the name
`iPhone 17 Pro`, so a bare `name=` destination is ambiguous.

## Commits
Do NOT commit automatically after a green build. Commit only when Brian asks,
and then as one shippable commit per fix — stage the exact files that fix
touched, never `git add -A`. (Same discipline as the review overlay's
review-only default, `.cursor/skills/chromaglow-code-quality-review/SKILL.md`.)

## Common Build Errors
- "Cannot find type 'X'" → File not added to pbxproj. See xcode-project.mdc.
- "Argument passed to call that takes no arguments" → Check method signatures in existing code, don't guess.
- "Type 'StudioStrategy' does not conform to 'Equatable'" → Already fixed. It's Equatable now.
